## Overview

|                    |                                                     |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| **Release**        | :badge[Q4 2026]{color=teal}                         |
| **Health**         | :status[On track]{color=green}                      |
| **Build progress** | :progress{value=35}                                 |
| **Design**         | [Figma — Saved searches](https://example.com/figma) |

Power users re-run the same 3–5 searches every day. Saving them removes [~40 seconds]{weight=bold} per search and lets us notify people when something new appears.

:::question Open question
Should saved searches be shareable with a team in v1, or only personal? *Decision needed by 2026-10-10.*
:::

## Requirements

::::tabs
:::tab Must have
- [x] Save the current query and filters with a name
- [ ] List, rename and delete saved searches
- [ ] Daily email digest when new results match
:::
:::tab Nice to have
- [ ] Share with a team
- [ ] Slack notifications
:::
:::tab Out of scope
- Real-time push notifications
- Saved searches on mobile (Q1 2027)
:::
::::

## User flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[Search page] -->|Save search| N[Name it]
    N --> L[(Saved searches)]
    L -->|nightly job| J{New matches?}
    J -- yes --> E[Email digest]
    J -- no --> X[Do nothing]
```

## API

:::::columns
::::column{width=55%}
```http title="Create"
POST /v1/saved-searches
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Open P1 bugs", "query": "priority:p1 state:open" }
```
::::
::::column
:::card{accent=teal} Limits
- 50 saved searches per user
- Name ≤ 80 characters
- Digest at 08:00 in the user's time zone
:::
::::
:::::

:::warning Breaking change
`GET /v1/search` will require the `filters` object instead of query-string filters. Clients must migrate before **2026-11-01**.
:::

## Rollout

```mermaid
gantt
    dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD
    section Build
    API & storage      :a1, 2026-10-01, 14d
    UI                 :a2, after a1, 10d
    section Launch
    Internal beta      :b1, after a2, 7d
    GA                 :milestone, after b1, 0d
```

:::agent Implementation guidance
- Store saved searches in the existing `user_prefs` Postgres schema; do **not** add a new database.
- Reuse `SearchQuery.parse()` for validation — never hand-parse query strings.
- Every new endpoint needs an OpenAPI entry in `api/openapi.yaml` and a contract test.
- If the open question above is still unresolved, implement personal-only saved searches.
:::

:::human Why an agent block?
Coding agents read the block above as constraints. People can skim past it — it's collapsed in the preview.
:::
